            <td data-label="Role"><strong>{item.role}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Requirement">{item.requirement}</td>
            <td data-label="Reality">{item.reality}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take: FSSAI eligibility is narrower than most students assume</p>
    <p>
      Food Safety Officer and Technical Officer notifications from FSSAI often specifically favour food technology or dairy technology degrees.
    </p>
    <p>
      A general home science or nutrition degree is not always on the eligible list for every posting. Read the actual current notification before planning a career around this route, rather than assuming any home-science-adjacent degree qualifies.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Where multi-stage competition genuinely applies here is the CDPO route specifically: a graduate needs to clear a state Public Service Commission selection process for a limited number of seats, and promotion up the ladder afterward runs into its own competitive bottlenecks. Anganwadi Worker and Helper posts, by contrast, are locally recruited and not part of that same competitive exam ladder.
  </p>

  <p>
    Pay is structured and predictable — an FSSAI Technical Officer's gross salary runs close to ₹74,000 a month at Level-7, with the usual central government allowances on top — but it is fixed by the pay scale, not by your own output. That is the honest trade-off of this track: real stability, genuinely capped growth.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hospitality">Hospitality and institutional catering management</h2>

  <p>
    Home science's resource-management and food-production training feeds directly into hospitality, hotel food and beverage operations, and institutional catering for hospitals, schools, and corporate cafeterias.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    For a full breakdown of the hotel-management side of this, read <a href="/blog/career-options/hotel-management-career-india-scope-and-salary/">hotel management career in India: scope and salary</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    The daily reality includes shifts, physical stamina, vendor negotiation, and cost control under real pressure — not just menu planning. The upside is that the same skills scale directly into owning a catering business, one of the more common self-employment routes for people who come out of this specialisation with real operational experience.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ownership">The ownership route: building a nutrition, food, or design business</h2>

  <p>
    This is worth pulling out on its own, because it is the single most under-discussed part of a home science career in India.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>Three genuinely scalable-ownership paths exist inside this field: a nutrition or dietetics private practice, a food or catering business, and a personal textile or design label.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      Each one scales for the same underlying reason — you control pricing and can grow beyond one person's working hours through repeat clients, a growing team, or digital reach, instead of trading a fixed number of hours for a fixed salary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    A nutrition practice scales through recurring client relationships and, increasingly, through online consultations and content that reach clients well beyond one city. A food or catering business scales through repeat orders, product lines, and eventually hiring and systemising production. A design label scales through an online store, a growing customer base, and a recognisable style that does not depend on one wholesale buyer.
  </p>

  <p>
    None of these are guaranteed outcomes. All three demand real business skill on top of the domain skill: pricing, positioning, client acquisition, and the discipline to treat the work like a business, not a hobby with invoices.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    If you are trying to work out which of these three ownership routes actually fits your strengths, money runway, and risk tolerance, that comparison is exactly what a structured <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career counselling and career guidance</a> conversation is built for — it is faster than guessing and re-guessing on your own for a year.
  </p>

