  </p>

  <p>
    Use the conservative starting benchmark of roughly 10% of your total education budget on college itself, with the rest reserved for tools, internships, projects, certifications, and the proof of work that actually gets you hired or trusted with clients. Spending materially more only makes sense with a specific, verified reason.
